{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/678701-restoring-the-wyrm-to-sanity","id":678701,"title":"Restoring the Wyrm to Sanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-26T03:43:35-07:00","id":678701,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Restoring the Wyrm to Sanity","content":"How would you go about it? Keep in mind that this isn't a setting hack; convincing the Wyrm not be corrosive to existence, do it's job and not kill Gaia outright is closest thing to stopping the apocalypse as can be done. This doesn't remove Pentex (but one might have to do so first) or the BSD or anything else.<br /> <br /> Just very simply, how would/should you go about making the Wyrm not crazy or having multiple personalities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T04:26:38-07:00","id":678762,"title":"","content":"i would think you would basically have to kill it. the wyrms own job is supposed to be to kill stuff so new stuff can come and see whats going on, it seems right that you would have to kill it yourself to have it come back as what its supposed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T07:55:22-07:00","id":679022,"title":"","content":"It's the possible result of the Weaver Ascendant scenario in Apocalypse. The rite to heal it, however, is at difficulty 10 (8 for a Gurahl ritemaster), requires 1000 points of permanent Gnosis, and lots of successes, all while being performed in Malfeas with a huge battle going on in the entire realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T08:47:06-07:00","id":679061,"title":"","content":"If the Wyrm has gone mad from the webs of the Weaver, then would doing enough damage to the Weaver's creations have a positibility of freeing the Wyrm? Would freeing the Wyrm this way restore it's sanity or just give us a more powerful insane Wyrm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T09:37:08-07:00","id":679126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/678701-restoring-the-wyrm-to-sanity?p=679061#post679061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Wyrm has gone mad from the webs of the Weaver, then would doing enough damage to the Weaver's creations have a positibility of freeing the Wyrm? Would freeing the Wyrm this way restore it's sanity or just give us a more powerful insane Wyrm?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're taking that too literally. We're talking about a metaphysical attempt to bind the Wyrm. It's not a historical event that can be mapped out to Earth and mankind, and removing all of the Weaver influence on Earth would barely dent the Weaver in its totality.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T11:32:23-07:00","id":679199,"title":"","content":"Freeing the Wyrm is giving it back its sanity. Now to free the Wyrm there are many solutions<br /> <br /> 1 Kill Weaver Incarnas and Celestines, that would damage the Pattern Web<br /> 2 Free the queen of the spider-shifters of her opal prison in Malfeas<br /> 3 Dance the Ninth Circle of the Spiral and do what Hakaken and Number Two didn't do<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T14:30:26-07:00","id":679332,"title":"","content":"Is it even possible? I mean, we are talking about a being intertwined with fabric of reality on a cosmic level. It's beyond colossal. Would it even notice an attack by a pack of werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T16:16:31-07:00","id":679426,"title":"","content":"I doubt it. To be noticed you have to do as mentioned before, hit the 9th circle and ascend. Would take a true hero of gaia to do that and not go corrupt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T17:49:15-07:00","id":679486,"title":"","content":"I think that is very possible to restore the sanity of the Wyrm concluding an apocalypse chronicle with some kind of mass ritual or even delving into the Weavers domains to losen the end driving the Wyrm mad.<br /> <br /> While a noble goal it would be a hard sell as a sane Wyrm would take one look at the world as it is at the moment and would destroy it as being tainted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T21:04:32-07:00","id":679611,"title":"","content":"Oh, it's a extremely hard sell, though I don't think the Wyrm would destroy the entire world right away. <i><b>Corrupted</b></i> Wyrm-tainted things would go first, (bye-bye Pentex) followed by Evil Weaver stuff...after that it might calm down a bit.<br /> <br /> Unless I'm mistaken, if any of the Triat dies, the world is doomed as without them certain concepts of reality stop being 'pushed'. So ultimately the Wyrm needs to be brought back into the fold. None of the Garou nation have seemed to pick up on this or they have written bit of as a necessary evil; an Apocalypse if you will.<br /> <br /> Hence why I'm soliciting ideas for how to get the Big Bad back to 'normal'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T03:03:26-07:00","id":679814,"title":"","content":"Oh I'm pretty sure the Garou know that killing the Wyrm is impossible and that they would need to fix it to have a good end. It's just that they have been fighting such a war against such things that they don't really see how either of those options are actually feasible. Not that a dedicated band of PC's might not find a way....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T10:58:09-07:00","id":683297,"title":"","content":"I remember in the Nuwisha Breedbook, that the Wyrm &quot;just has to ask&quot; and Coyote would tell him how to escape the Weaver's webs. Maybe it could be possible (but very hard) to restore some aspect that could ask for help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T22:41:44-07:00","id":683951,"title":"","content":"An idea? Free it? <br /> <br /> It immediately begins to reknit, between the Defiler, The Eater of souls and Beast of War, back into the Wyrm of Balance.<br /> <br /> but its a question of how long it takes, will the first thing the Wyrm Sees when it regains lucidity, be Gaia's corpse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T01:27:15-07:00","id":684084,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm is quite free. The whole point is that the Weaver couldn't contain the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T02:17:12-07:00","id":684105,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression the Wyrm could not freely act in the manner it was supposed too because the Weaver bound it. Being bound drove it to insanity and autocannibalism, which led to new behaviours that <i><b>weren't bound. </b></i>Hence why captain balance is 'RAR, corruption, yeah!', it is the only way it can do anything and if it was in it's right mind it would purge itself as unclean and dangerous.<br /> <br /> The whole tragic point of the Wyrm is that it is not in it's right mind; all it's followers are based on that fallacy. Whether it is 'it gives me power to pursue my own goals', 'it is futile to fight it', 'I have no other viable choice', 'I was born in to it', or any of the other excuses and justifications when it comes down to it they are working for an illogical end no-one really wants. Pentex &amp; the BSD aren't generally shown as nihilists but that is the end goal. The sad irony is that 95% percent of Wyrm's armies doesn't want the world to end, and I'm pretty sure that deep down that includes the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Now I can be wholly wrong in why musings, but please correct me on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T02:53:53-07:00","id":684131,"title":"","content":"When the Weaver tried to contain the Wyrm so that it would adhere to its plan and schedule it tried to do the impossible. Irresistible Force meeting a Immovable object. So when it wrapped up the Wyrm in its webs, the Wyrm broke free. The problem is that when they hit each other they fucked each other up. While we are talking about cosmic principles, you can pretty much sum it up as both of them going kookoo. Weaver was already fixated on keeping its perfect creations forever the same, so that just got worse. The Wyrm on the other hand fractured. Note that the whole of existence needs the Wyrm to actually exist, and the Wyrm still does most of its work as it used to, or we wouldn't have a normal circle of life.<br /> <br /> The problem is with the fractures. You can imagine it like a horrifying wound that got horribly infected and bloated. And from that wound seeps hate, disgust and a desire to end everything in as much pain and suffering as is possible. Any point where you actually try to &quot;fix&quot; the Wyrm starts with actually getting that wound to heal. Until it does out of it seeps poison, death and murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:13:34-07:00","id":684353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/678701-restoring-the-wyrm-to-sanity?p=684105#post684105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression the Wyrm could not freely act in the manner it was supposed too because the Weaver bound it. Being bound drove it to insanity and autocannibalism, which led to new behaviours that <i><b>weren't bound. </b></i>Hence why captain balance is 'RAR, corruption, yeah!', it is the only way it can do anything and if it was in it's right mind it would purge itself as unclean and dangerous.<br /> <br /> The whole tragic point of the Wyrm is that it is not in it's right mind; all it's followers are based on that fallacy. Whether it is 'it gives me power to pursue my own goals', 'it is futile to fight it', 'I have no other viable choice', 'I was born in to it', or any of the other excuses and justifications when it comes down to it they are working for an illogical end no-one really wants. Pentex &amp; the BSD aren't generally shown as nihilists but that is the end goal. The sad irony is that 95% percent of Wyrm's armies doesn't want the world to end, and I'm pretty sure that deep down that includes the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Now I can be wholly wrong in why musings, but please correct me on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just pro-Wyrm propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T06:28:50-07:00","id":684362,"title":"","content":"&quot;They're crazy&quot; makes more sense than &quot;they are stupid&quot; and &quot;just because&quot; is a really weak motivation.<br /> Besides, I'm not saying that's right; I'm inviting you to tell me where I went wrong. I'm very much aware that it would be suicide to say such things to a Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:00:32-07:00","id":684440,"title":"","content":"Actually your explanation is used in the 2nd Edition Book of he Wyrm. The Urges Wyrm are the product of the bound Wyrm's suffering and they are not bound to the Pattern Web<br /> <br /> In the novel Apocalypse it is implied that the goal of the Dance of Betrayal is to obtain a Black Spiral Dancer mighty enough to kill the Wyrm and thus restore it to a purer form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:06:37-07:00","id":684443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/678701-restoring-the-wyrm-to-sanity?p=684440#post684440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually your explanation is used in the 2nd Edition Book of he Wyrm. The Urges Wyrm are the product of the bound Wyrm's suffering and they are not bound to the Pattern Web<br /> <br /> In the novel Apocalypse it is implied that the goal of the Dance of Betrayal is to obtain a Black Spiral Dancer mighty enough to kill the Wyrm and thus restore it to a purer form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Novels and other fiction aren't canon. Remember when an Uktena metis got an Imbued woman pregnant? Also a novel. A Garou that was also a Bastet? In an anthology or novel. Not things that actually stay with the setting as integrated parts of it, but they are in fiction for the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:14:11-07:00","id":684456,"title":"","content":"Novels aren't canon sure but the implication of the Ninth Circle seems sound. Why else the ultimate level of enlightnement in the Wyrm's service would be called &quot;Betrayal&quot;?<br /> <br /> And while the novels are not canon, the cosmology chapter of Book of the Wyrm 2nd that indicates the ultimate Wyrm wants to die is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T08:21:42-07:00","id":684470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/678701-restoring-the-wyrm-to-sanity?p=684456#post684456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Novels aren't canon sure but the implication of the Ninth Circle seems sound. Why else the ultimate level of enlightnement in the Wyrm's service would be called &quot;Betrayal&quot;?<br /> <br /> And while the novels are not canon, the cosmology chapter of Book of the Wyrm 2nd that indicates the ultimate Wyrm wants to die is.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things you don't want to do in a game is completely undercut the normal play experience, and making that the goal would be it. The BSDs also aren't inclined to help anyone or anything; one of them killing the Wyrm would probably result in shutting shit down for good, slowly and as painfully as possible, not a period of renewal and eventual recovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T17:17:59-07:00","id":686281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/678701-restoring-the-wyrm-to-sanity?p=684443#post684443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Garou that was also a Bastet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where? How? That sounds laughably bad.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T21:21:02-07:00","id":686451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/678701-restoring-the-wyrm-to-sanity?p=686281#post686281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where? How? That sounds laughably bad.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was in the 1st short story anthology. However as I recall the girl in question was pre change and kin to both Werewolves and Bastet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T21:40:34-07:00","id":686456,"title":"","content":"I always treat these metaphysical explanations of the game lightly and not too seriously. Rather than being something that is &quot;true&quot;, it just seems something some Garou theologians came up with to resolve the Problem of Evil that all religions have to contend with.<br /> <br /> <i>Garou Theurge: Gaia is perfect.<br /> <br /> Garou cub: Then why are there all these bad things happening?<br /> <br /> Garou Theurge: Because there is this creature called the Wyrm that is the source of all evil.<br /> <br /> Garou cub: Why is there the Wyrm?<br /> <br /> Garou Theurge: Um, it is part of the Triat. It is one of the three things that made Gaia.<br /> <br /> Garou cub: How could something that is evil make Gaia?<br /> <br /> Garou Theurge: Um, because it wasn't evil to begin with.<br /> <br /> Garou cub: Then how did it become evil?<br /> <br /> Garou Theurge: Um, because something else made it evil by mistake.<br /> <br /> Garou cub: What was that?<br /> <br /> Garou Theurge: Um... The Weaver! It trapped the Wyrm in its webs, and the Wyrm went mad trying to get out.<br /> <br /> Garou cub: Then why...<br /> <br /> Garou Theurge: Our time is now over. It's time for you to start learning about the Litany. Go talk to the Philodox.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T22:14:35-07:00","id":686497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/678701-restoring-the-wyrm-to-sanity?p=686456#post686456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always treat these metaphysical explanations of the game lightly and not too seriously. Rather than being something that is &quot;true&quot;, it just seems something some Garou theologians came up with to resolve the Problem of Evil that all religions have to contend with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cubs probably wouldn't be getting a talk with details like that. The story about the Wyrm's imprisonment tend to be things that even most Theurges might be unaware; the real deal is given out of character, after all. It's sort of like how not many people are actually supposed to know about Pentex or its role in tying together most of those subsidiaries, only on a larger scale.<br /> <br /> Of course, the number one detail that a Theurge might not actually give is starting with &quot;Gaia is perfect&quot;, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T04:06:37-07:00","id":686780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/678701-restoring-the-wyrm-to-sanity?p=686497#post686497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cubs probably wouldn't be getting a talk with details like that. The story about the Wyrm's imprisonment tend to be things that even most Theurges might be unaware; the real deal is given out of character, after all. It's sort of like how not many people are actually supposed to know about Pentex or its role in tying together most of those subsidiaries, only on a larger scale.<br /> <br /> Of course, the number one detail that a Theurge might not actually give is starting with &quot;Gaia is perfect&quot;, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Sorry, but the Garou are a culture stemmed in Oral tradition. They have stories about stories. They would sure as hell not be caught with their pants down when presenting the cosmology to young ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}